      questions:[Q(0,90,"Is Zerg building economy, speed, or immediate units?","The same Hatchery count can hide radically different larva allocation.","Count what larva becomes, not only the number of Hatcheries."),Q(90,190,"What does Zerg need to defend my first credible threat?","A threat can be valuable even without damage if it forces Queens, Lings, Spores, or Roaches instead of Drones.","Pressure can tax future economy without winning a fight."),Q(190,290,"Do I need information air, mobile Gateway pressure, or stable Robo splash?","The tech choice should answer the Zerg allocation you actually observed.","Do not counter a composition that has not been purchased yet."),Q(290,410,"Can my third survive the next larva cycle?","Zerg can convert larvae to army rapidly; a safe third needs advance warning and reinforcement geometry.","A worker lead is only real if it survives the next army cycle."),Q(410,9999,"What would make my current army obsolete?","Lurkers, Mutas, mass Ravager, Hive tech, and explosive Drone growth all invalidate different assumptions.","Re-scout the transition, not merely the current army.")],
