      questions:[Q(0,95,"What does my first scout need to prove before I schedule the next pressure?","Reaper information determines whether the next cycle can be economic or must respect aggression.","A schedule without scouting becomes a script."),Q(95,210,"Can my pressure force army larva without donating units?","The objective is often to tax Drone production, not to kill a Hatchery.","Damage includes units the opponent was forced to build."),Q(210,330,"Should my next capability be Bio mobility, Tank stability, or air reach?","The correct production mix depends on creep, Zerg tech, and how much territory must be defended.","Production structures are commitments to future cycles."),Q(330,470,"Can I add the third CC while my current threat keeps Zerg honest?","The cheaper 300-mineral CC rewards compounding behind credible pressure, but not if the army disappears.","Expand behind a tax, not behind hope."),Q(470,9999,"Where will the next Zerg army appear faster than my production can rotate?","Creep, Nydus, Mutas, and multi-prong attacks punish slow response geometry.","Terran schedules must include defense travel time." )],
