      questions:[Q(0,95,"What Protoss investment is the first Reaper trying to reveal?","Nexus, Gateway count, and tech location define the first danger window.","The Reaper buys information first and damage second."),Q(95,215,"What is the first Protoss power spike and when does it become dangerous?","Blink, Oracle, Robo, and fast splash create different movement rules.","Name the spike before planning the fight."),Q(215,330,"Can I threaten two places before demanding a frontal win?","Protoss expensive units are strongest when concentrated.","Movement can be a damage source even without kills."),Q(330,460,"Can my third CC grow behind a threat Protoss must respect?","The economic investment is safest when Protoss cannot freely cross the map with its full army.","Expand behind tempo or defensive geometry."),Q(460,9999,"Which Protoss unit must I preserve my answer for?","Colossi, Disruptors, Templar, Blink armies, and air transitions each punish a different careless trade.","Do not spend the counter on the wrong target." )],
      branches:[B("bio","Bio / Medivac mobility","Repeatable pressure, multi-prong threat, and production scaling.","Choose when you can force Protoss to move before its splash ball is perfectly assembled.","Requires upgrades, Medivac preservation, and disciplined splitting.","Threaten secondary locations, pre-split, and avoid fighting concentrated splash on its terms.","Bio collapses when every fight is frontal into full Protoss power."),B("mine","Mine / tempo control","Area denial, drop threat, and a way to force detection/positioning responses.","Choose when mobility and attention tax can delay Protoss's clean tech/economy progression.","Can lose value against prepared detection and careful control.","Use Mines to shape movement, not only chase worker kills.","Repeated predictable Mine drops become negative tempo."),B("tank-raven","Tank/Raven stability","Defensive and push geometry, anti-tech utility, and a way to anchor against concentrated ground power.","Choose when the game is about holding or creating a specific siege lane rather than constant mobility.","Slower rotations and expensive gas.","Control vision, protect Tanks, and make Protoss walk through an unfair zone.","Do not drag the siege army through open ground without information." )],
